From: LightMoss <lightmoss@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: r36sclone: the blue LED is off released

The blue front LED that stands in for the rumble motor is dark only
while gpio0 PA0 is not driven, as builds that never touched the pin left
it. Driven low (GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH at rest) it was on all the time and went
dark only for a rumble; driven high at rest (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW) it was
reported on as well. rumble-gpio-hiz-off (the joypad patch after this)
releases the pin when no effect plays; an effect drives it low.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
@@ -68,12 +68,19 @@
 		/*
 		 * The G80CA has no rumble motor. Its blue front LED (gpio0 PA0,
 		 * arkos4clone's led-blue) stands in for one, the way spruce blinks
-		 * the LED on the MagicX Zero 28: the driver drives this pin while a
-		 * force-feedback effect plays, so spruce's vibrate (Game Switcher,
-		 * held power/menu buttons, low battery) and game rumble light it.
-		 * Off otherwise, after the driver's 1 s rumble at probe.
+		 * the LED on the MagicX Zero 28: lit while a force-feedback effect
+		 * plays (spruce's vibrate: Game Switcher, held power/menu buttons, low
+		 * battery; game rumble), and for a second when the joypad probes at
+		 * boot. Off otherwise, asleep included.
+		 *
+		 * Off is the pin released (an input), as builds that never touched
+		 * it left it: the LED was dark there. Driven, it was seen lit: on
+		 * a G80CA-MB, driven low it was on for good (it went dark only
+		 * while the pin was driven high for a rumble), and with the pin
+		 * driven high at rest it was reported on as well. On drives it low.
 		 */
-		rumble-gpio = <&gpio0 RK_PA0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		rumble-gpio = <&gpio0 RK_PA0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		rumble-gpio-hiz-off;
 
 		/* gpio pincontrol setup */
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
